map.summary:
The October records show where real catches came from. In-repo traces 2026-10-17..27 and RUN_STATE items 37-78 (33 magistrate activations, 2 loop wakes, 5 interactive sessions) record roughly 55-60 cold or blind seat runs in 13 days (my count from the cited records; the exact total is INFERRED). Two kinds of check found every defect that touched data:

(1) **Executing reviews and cold passes.** These are the only gates that caught defects that would have changed a number from real program output:
- the #416 audit found the NEG-8 reference span (B was 52 % too low);
- the PR #501 cold passes found two MAJORs that decided which runs count;
- the #573 delta pass found the twin diverging on compressed input (185 fields above the bar);
- the B2-NR1 pass found M1, the C_j form;
- the KB cold passes found two class-changing corrections;
- the b6 acceptance judges found the S-8 exclusion would remove 14 of 53 known-good runs, and changed c_q from 0.73 to 0.54.

(2) **Real-program rehearsals.** Machine tests 1 and 2, the H arm refusals and the s1-p1 run found every defect that would have refused or emptied sessions. Each of those had already passed every review. The worst case: s1-p1's missing plan_tree.sha256 sidecars got past the #416 triple audit, 7 cold delta rounds, the registration gate and CI. The defect class was the same as machine test 1's.

What found nothing that touched a number:
- the gate-ledger format checker and the docs-freshness fences;
- the four-model council, which never ran;
- per-rule cold judges (no W catch in three periods, per the pruning list);
- registration whole-file gates (text corrections only);
- delta rounds after the cause of a defect class was found (#416 rounds 4-7: "edge cases that cannot occur on the real records", about 5 h and 8 seats).

**Minimal gate set that keeps the science protections:**
- **(a) One stage of two blind executing seats from different model families, run in parallel.** These count as both review and cold pass for code that decides counting, exclusion or estimators. One family is enough for other full-tier code.
- **(b) Delta passes stop under a written rule.** The same defect class twice goes straight to a structural ruling. A round with only LOW/INFO findings, or findings no real archive can reach (replayed over every archive), ends the chain.
- **(c) A mandatory non-claim real-loop smoke on committed bytes** before a registered pack's first counting session.
- **(d) Kept as they are:** the independent recompute as the only release arithmetic check; blinding; the agent census and battery float.
- **(e) CI with only number-protecting checks blocking.**
- **(f) One executing refuter plus a recorded line replaces per-rule cold judges.** This was decided 10-14 (7a decision 3) but never written into jw:docs/orchestration.md.
- **(g) Removed or lightened:** block-5 step 12, block-6 §13's full-size synthetic chain, and the release cold gate that the scout added against block-6 §12.3.

**Placement.** The measurement Mac should only measure, harvest and run the block-5 dry run. Agent presence on the Mac cost at least 9.5 h of idle Mac time plus a lost session (s6-p1) and two withdrawn machine-test installs in October. Moving orchestration (the magistrate) to the MacBook Air removes that hazard at its source. The Air can also:
- hold the ChatGPT login for the Codex Cloud launcher;
- run local Sol seats when Codex Cloud has no executors, as on 10-22 and 10-23;
- run the macOS whole suite, which matches the measurement Mac's platform.

Reviews, councils, refuters, fix seats, synthetic tests and CI stay in the cloud.

**Compliance gap.** TIER-01's day-30 review was due 2026-10-25. jw:docs/process/tier01_defect_log.md is empty, and jw:docs/decision_log.md ends at D-186 (09-29), so the light tier lapsed under its own text. It should be renewed now on a recorded escape count of zero.

