Not on the Air: real claim-data analysis, until cadence plan item 2.4 removes the host-speed dependence. The Air is passively cooled, so sustained-load throughput is INFERRED to be lower and the 120 s deadline would be more likely to fire.

**CLOUD (Claude seats 4 vCPU/15 GB; Codex Cloud 5 vCPU/17 GB; GitHub hosted CI):**
- every review, cold pass, delta pass, council seat, refuter and judge;
- fix and build seats (L9-2, B6-AN-1);
- synthetic tests, including the one cached full-size test_dry_run;
- the scout and brief drafting;
- CI.

This is 'as much in the cloud as possible' (Ed). Cloud seats are already the default (item 39). Their weak points are outages (10-22/23) and the 2 h background cap on locally launched seats (7209d1b0 item 12). An orchestrator on the Air, re-seating from pushed branches, absorbs both.
